<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Marcopolo raised.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Marcopolo raised.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Deutsche Morgan Grenfell analyst Raquel Abud on Wednesday raised her rating on Brazil's Marcopolo Marcopolo SA Carroceria e Onibus to hold from sell.</p>
<p>-- &quot;Due to its recent underperformance ... we are upgrading our recommendation to hold,&quot; Abud wrote in a report.</p>
<p>-- &quot;We believe that Marcopolo deserves a lower P/E than the private sector average, as it does not show any increase in results for the next two years.&quot;</p>
<p>-- &quot;Our target price for this stock is $200/1,000 shares.&quot;</p>
<p>-- The company's preferred shares closed Tuesday in Sao Paulo at 180.1 reais.</p>
<p>((--Ian Simpson, Wall Street Desk, (212) 859-1879))</p>
